": "A hypothetical entity with special abilities postulated for the sake of a thought experiment in philosophy or physics.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Let the orders now be that each demon is to stop all molecules from crossing his area in either direction except 100 coming from A, arbitrarily chosen to be let pass into B, and a greater number, having among them less energy but equal momentum, to cross from B to A.", "reference": "1874, William Thomson, 1st Baron Kelvin, “Kinetic Theory of the Dissipation of Energy” in Nature 9, 441-444"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}]}, {"definition": "Someone with great strength, passion or skill for a particular activity, pursuit etc.; an enthusiast.", "tags": [], "examples": ["He’s a demon at the card tables."], "quotes": [{"text": "Chelsea defended like demons to snuff out Manchester City but this was a perfectly calibrated triumph, built upon a structured attacking approach, choosing the right moments to transition, and illuminated by the smoothness of Havertz’s technique.", "reference": "2021 May 29, David Hytner, “Chelsea win Champions League after Kai Havertz stuns Manchester City”, in The Guardian:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(card games) A type of patience or solitaire (card game) played in the UK and/or US.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "‘That's much the best feeling to have.’ She dealt out the first row of ‘demon’.", "reference": "1924, EM Forster, A Passage to India, Penguin, published 2005, page 89:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "Any of various hesperiid butterflies of the genera Notocrypta and Udaspes.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": ["genius", "tutelary deity", "barghest", "bogie", "bogeyman", "boggard", "bogle", "cacodem